│ Okay, let’s address this. I’ve determined that the core issue is a │
│ misunderstanding of how Django’s model methods are called and how  │
│ get_FIELD_display() behaves. Specifically, Django 2.2+ changed the │
│ behavior of get_FIELD_display() to return a string representation  │
│ of the field value directly, rather than calling a separate        │
│ display method. The original code was attempting to override a     │
│ method that no longer existed in the same way.                     │
│                                                                    │
│ The fix is to remove the attempt to override get_FIELD_display()   │
│ and instead rely on Django’s default behavior.  We should also     │
│ ensure that the __str__ method returns the correct display value.  │
│                                                                    │
│ Here’s the patch:                                                  │
│                                                                    │
│ ┏━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━┓ │
